| ShortSummary    = After developing metal-bending abilities, [[Joey Gutierrez (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Joey Gutierrez]] is saved from the hostile [[Advanced Threat Containment Unit]] (ATCU)—[[President of the United States|President]] [[Matthew Ellis (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Matthew Ellis]]' replacement for the underground [[S.H.I.E.L.D.]]—by S.H.I.E.L.D. agents. When Agent [[Daisy Johnson (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Daisy Johnson]] struggles to explain to Gutierrez their [[Inhumans (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Inhuman]] heritage, activated by exposure to the recently released compound [[Terrigen]], she seeks the help of [[Lincoln Campbell]], who taught her but now wants to live a normal life. S.H.I.E.L.D. Director [[Phil Coulson]] finds the leader of the ATCU, [[Rosalind Price]], and the two realize that there is a third party interested in new Inhumans: the monstrous Inhuman [[Lash (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Lash]], who attacks Daisy and Lincoln. The subsequent arrival of the ATCU causes both Lash and Lincoln to flee; the organization begins hunting them. Agent [[Leo Fitz]] acquires an ancient Hebrew scroll describing the [[Kree (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Kree]] Monolith—that consumed his partner [[Jemma Simmons]]—as "Death" ({{langx|he|מות}}), which Fitz is unable to accept. Simmons, meanwhile, is on a desolate alien planet.
| LineColor       = BEBEBE
