| Viewers         = 4.32<ref name="302Ratings">{{Cite web |last=Porter |first=Rick |date=October 7, 2015 |title=Tuesday final ratings: 'The Muppets,' 'NCIS' and 'Scream Queens' adjusted up, 'Flash' and 'iZombie' hold |url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2015/10/07/tuesday-final-ratings-oct-6-2015/477169/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151007222144/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2015/10/07/tuesday-final-ratings-oct-6-2015/477169/ |archive-date=October 7, 2015 |access-date=October 7, 2015 |website=[[TV by the Numbers]]}}</ref>
| ShortSummary    = Dr. [[Andrew Garner]] evaluates Gutierrez and deems him not yet ready to join the Secret Warriors, Daisy's potential team of Inhumans. [[Grant Ward (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Grant Ward]], looking to rebuild [[Hydra (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Hydra]], recruits [[Werner von Strucker (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Werner von Strucker]], son of previous leader Baron [[Wolfgang von Strucker (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Wolfgang von Strucker]]. Tasked with hunting down and killing Ward, Agent [[Lance Hunter (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Lance Hunter]] tracks down Garner's ex-wife Agent [[Melinda May]], who has been on leave from S.H.I.E.L.D. for six months. May is convinced not to run from her life, despite difficulties in her relationships with Garner and Coulson, and eventually agrees to join Hunter in his mission. Fitz realizes that the Monolith is a portal and S.H.I.E.L.D. enlists [[Asgard (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Asgardian]] [[Elliot Randolph]]. Randolph takes them to an old English castle, where a now-deteriorated machine was constructed to open the Monolith using vibrations. Daisy is able to replicate this effect with her abilities and Fitz sends a flare through before entering the portal himself. He finds Simmons and is able to bring her back just as Daisy's power destroys the Monolith.
| LineColor       = BEBEBE
}}
