| Viewers         = 3.20<ref name="314Ratings">{{Cite web |last=Porter |first=Rick |date=March 30, 2016 |title=Tuesday final ratings: 'The Voice' adjusts up, 'Chicago Fire' and 'Beyond the Tank' adjust down |url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2016/03/30/tuesday-final-ratings-march-29-16/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160402054331/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2016/03/30/tuesday-final-ratings-march-29-16/ |archive-date=April 2, 2016 |access-date=March 31, 2016 |website=[[TV by the Numbers]]}}</ref>
| ShortSummary    = Mack, struggling with the departures of Morse and Hunter, takes time off to be with his brother [[Ruben Mackenzie|Ruben]]. When an online hate group called the [[Watchdogs (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Watchdogs]] uses [[Howard Stark (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Howard Stark]]-developed nitramene bombs to perform a terrorist attack on an ATCU facility, Coulson suspects that former S.H.I.E.L.D. agent [[Felix Blake]]—who had been committed to the advancement of nitramene technology and has been missing since having his back broken by [[Mike Peterson (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Deathlok]]{{efn|As depicted in "[[End of the Beginning (Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.)|End of the Beginning]]".}}—has taken over the group. Ruben becomes disillusioned with Mack when he leaves to investigate a Watchdog base and accidentally reveals his S.H.I.E.L.D. agent status, but Mack is able to improve their relationship when he fends off a group of the terrorists that attack the brothers. Coulson takes Lincoln to search Blake's known safehouses and the two are confronted by Blake via hologram at one; he reveals that Hydra is backing him and the Watchdogs in their crusade to kill all Inhumans, and S.H.I.E.L.D. realizes that the attack was a cover for Hydra to steal something from the ATCU.
